## Layout recipes

The recipe layer turns ordinary semantic Carve into polished layouts without adding
parser extensions. The same source remains useful in Markdown and plain text.

### A connected project tree

{data-guides="dotted"}
::: tree
- coffee-guide/
  - beans/
    - ethiopia.crv
    - colombia.crv
  - recipes/
    - aeropress.crv
    - v60.crv
  - assets/
    - roast.svg
  - README.crv
:::

### Cards and badges

::: cards
- *Source-first* - one readable `.crv` file feeds every output.
- *Print-ready* - typography, color, diagrams, and page furniture are embedded.
- *Portable* - PHP and JavaScript backends produce the same document structure.
:::

Release status: [stable]{.badge data-tone="success"}, quality [verified]{.badge},
and output [PDF]{.badge data-tone="info"}.

### Columns and steps

{data-columns="3"}
::: columns
*Choose.* Pick a freshly roasted coffee whose origin and process sound interesting.

*Grind.* Start medium-fine, then change one variable at a time after tasting.

*Record.* Keep the ratio, temperature, time, and a short sensory note together.
:::

::: steps
1. Write semantic Carve.
2. Render it through the selected engine.
3. Inline the complete stylesheet and local media.
4. Wait for math, charts, and diagrams, then print.
:::

### Gallery, aside, and wide content

